From dcf292c634b3292e5bc86e9ca9975de2dde4a639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ac/fs/frd: handle calls made when enabling SpotPass

Disney Magical World's SpotPass setup (and games on the HLE friends
service) hit these unimplemented calls. Layouts are from 3dbrew.

- ac GetCurrentAPInfo (0x000E): returns the 0x34-byte AP info. While
  connected it describes a fixed virtual AP (SSID "Tangelo", locally
  administered BSSID); otherwise it is empty.
- ac GetNZoneApNumService (0x0011): returns the 0x24-byte Nintendo Zone
  info, always empty (no Nintendo Zone hotspots).
- fs CheckAuthorityToAccessExtSaveData (0x083D): answers "has access";
  Tangelo does not enforce extdata access rights.
- frd AttachToEventNotification (0x0020): keeps the event; it is never
  signalled since there is no friend server.

ac GetConnectingLocation (0x0014) is left on the fallback: it is
undocumented. ps VerifyRsaSha256 is left as is on purpose; it needs a
real implementation, not a stub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
